AutoSubduce -- Flag for autosubduction before the sagbi algorithm
*****************************************************************

Description
===========

Autosubduction is a procedure which performs subduction on a collection of ring
elements against each other, one at a time. This is typically performed on a
set of generators of a *note Subring: Subring, or *note SAGBIBasis:
SAGBIBasis,. The result of each subduction replaces the original element in the
collection and zeros are removed from the collection. If the elements form a
subalgebra basis, then the result of autosubduction is unique.

By default, the function *note sagbi: sagbi, performs autosubduction on the
generators of the given *note Subring: Subring, before starting the main
algorithm. Setting this flag to false sometimes results in a performance
improvement, but with a risk of including nonreduced or redundant generators.

