CheckFullIntersection -- Flag for deciding if isFullIntersection is called
**************************************************************************

Description
===========

If the option is set to true, then the function *note
intersect(Subring,Subring): intersect_lpSubring_cmSubring_rp, performs two
tests. If either of these tests fail, then a relevant warning message is
displayed. Other than the warning messages, the output of the function *note
intersect(Subring,Subring): intersect_lpSubring_cmSubring_rp, is not affected
by the value of this option. If the option CheckFullIntersection is set to
false then no warnings are produced.

The first test is performed at the beginning of the function call. It checks
whether any of the inputs is an *note intersected subring: IntersectedSubring,
and applies *note isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, to each instance. For
more details see *note isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection,. If the function
*note isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, returns false, i.e., the
generators of the input are not guaranteed to generate the full intersection,
then a warning is printed.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S1 = subring {x^2, y^2};                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S2 = subring {x*y};                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : gens (S3 = intersect(S1, S2, Limit => 6, CheckFullIntersection =>       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | x2y2 |                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|             1      1                                                        |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|false))                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isFullIntersection S3                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : gens (S4 = intersect(S3, S2, Limit => 6))                               |
|-- Warning! The input contains an IntersectedSubring whose generators may not|
|                                                                             |
|o6 = | x2y2 |                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|             1      1                                                        |
|o6 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|generate the entire subring                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isFullIntersection S4                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In the example above, a warning is produced when computing $S4$ because the
input algebra $S3$ is not guaranteed to be the full intersection. However, the
final line shows that the generators of $S4$ are guaranteed to generate the
full intersection of $S2$ and $S3$.

The second test is performed at the end of the function call. It checks if the
result is guaranteed to generate the full intersection by calling *note
isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, on the result. If the function *note
isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, returns false, then a warning printed.
For instance, in the example above, the computation of $S3$ would print a
warning.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : intersect(S1, S2, Limit => 6)                                   |
|-- Warning! Result is not a full intersection.  Try increasing Limit.|
|                                                                     |
|o8 = QQ[p_0], subring of R                                           |
|                                                                     |
|o8 : IntersectedSubring                                              |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

If this warning message appears, then it is recommended to set the option *note
SAGBILimitType: SAGBILimitType, to its default value of Fixed or to use a
higher value for the option *note Limit: Subduction computation limit,.

