generators(SAGBIBasis) -- Returns generators of a SAGBIBasis computation object
*******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note generators: (Macaulay2Doc)generators,
  * Usage: 
        result = gens S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CoefficientRing: (Macaulay2Doc)generators_lpRing_rp, => a *note
        Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value null, unused
        option
  * Outputs:
      * result, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

Returns a list of subalgebra generators of the *note Subring: Subring,
underlying the *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis,. If the subalgebra generators do
not form a complete subalgebra basis (for example if they were obtained from a
partial computation), then the generators obtained from this command may not be
a generating set for the original subring.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                    |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x*y, x^2*y, x^3*y};|
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : gens S                          |
|                                     |
|o3 = | xy x2y x3y |                  |
|                                     |
|             1      3                |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                 |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : SB = sagbi(S, Limit => 3);      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : gens SB                         |
|                                     |
|o5 = | xy x2y |                      |
|                                     |
|             1      2                |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                 |
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : isSAGBI S                       |
|                                     |
|o6 = true                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i7 : isSAGBI SB                      |
|                                     |
|o7 = false                           |
+-------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis, -- The type of all subalgebra bases
  * *note generators(Subring): generators_lpSubring_rp, -- A generating set of
    a subring
  * *note sagbi: sagbi, -- Compute a subalgebra basis (sagbi basis)

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note generators(SAGBIBasis): generators_lpSAGBIBasis_rp, -- Returns
    generators of a SAGBIBasis computation object
