GeneratorSymbol -- variables for the presentationRing
*****************************************************

Description
===========

A symbol to be used for variables of the *note presentationRing:
presentationRing,.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring({x^2, y^2, x*y}, GeneratorSymbol => f)|
|                                                       |
|o2 = QQ[f_1..f_3], subring of R                        |
|                                                       |
|o2 : Subring                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (x+y)^4 // S                                      |
|                                                       |
|      2    2                     2                     |
|o3 = f  + f  + 4f f  + 4f f  + 6f                      |
|      1    2     1 3     2 3     3                     |
|                                                       |
|o3 : QQ[f ..f ]                                        |
|         1   3                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

If a symbol is not specified, then the variables of the *note presentationRing:
presentationRing, are indexed from 0 and use the default symbol. If a symbol is
specified, then the indices start from 1.

See also
========

  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
  * *note subring: subring, -- Constructs a subring of a polynomial ring.
  * *note presentationRing: presentationRing, -- returns the presentation ring
    of a subring

Functions with optional argument named GeneratorSymbol:
=======================================================

  * "subring(...,GeneratorSymbol=>...)" -- see *note subring: subring, --
    Constructs a subring of a polynomial ring.

For the programmer
==================

The object *note GeneratorSymbol: GeneratorSymbol, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

