groebnerMembershipTest -- Extrinsic method for subring membership
*****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        result = groebnerMembershipTest(f, S)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * S, a *note subring: Subring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * result, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, which indicates
        if $f$ belongs to $S$.

Description
===========

Uses the extrinsic method (based on Groebner bases) to test membership of a
polynomial in a subring.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                 |
+----------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x^2 - x*y, x^4};|
+----------------------------------+
|i3 : f1 = x^2*y^2 - 2*x^3*y;      |
+----------------------------------+
|i4 : groebnerMembershipTest(f1, S)|
|                                  |
|o4 = true                         |
+----------------------------------+
|i5 : f2 = x^10;                   |
+----------------------------------+
|i6 : groebnerMembershipTest(f2, S)|
|                                  |
|o6 = false                        |
+----------------------------------+

If a subalgebra basis is known for $S$, then it is recommended to use *note
RingElement % Subring: Reduction in subrings, instead.

See also
========

  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
  * *note RingElement % Subring: Reduction in subrings, -- Remainder modulo a
    subring
  * *note groebnerSubductionQuotient: groebnerSubductionQuotient, -- Extrinsic
    method for subduction quotients
  * *note RingElement // Subring: RingElement // Subring, -- Subduction
    quotient with respect to a subring
  * *note sagbi: sagbi, -- Compute a subalgebra basis (sagbi basis)

Ways to use groebnerMembershipTest:
===================================

