groebnerSubductionQuotient -- Extrinsic method for subduction quotients
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        result = groebnerSubductionQuotient(f, S)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * S, a *note subring: Subring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * result, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the normal
        form of $f$ in the *note presentationRing: presentationRing,

Description
===========

Uses the extrinsic method to compute a subduction quotient of $f$ by the
generators of $S$. A subduction quotient is an element of the *note
presentationRing: presentationRing,. The variables of this ring correspond to
the generators of $S$. A subduction quotient is a polynomial representation of
$f - f\%S$ in terms of the generators of $S$. The value of this element in the
*note ambient(Subring): ambient_lpSubring_rp, ring can be recovered using the
field presentationMap of the subring.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x+y, x*y, x*y^2};       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = x^3;                             |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f - (f%S)                            |
|                                          |
|      3    2        2    3                |
|o4 = x  + x y + 2x*y  + y                 |
|                                          |
|o4 : R                                    |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : gs = groebnerSubductionQuotient(f, S)|
|                                          |
|      3                                   |
|o5 = p  - 2p p  + p                       |
|      0     0 1    2                      |
|                                          |
|o5 : QQ[p ..p ]                           |
|         0   2                            |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : S#"presentationMap" gs               |
|                                          |
|      3    2        2    3                |
|o6 = x  + x y + 2x*y  + y                 |
|                                          |
|o6 : R                                    |
+------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
  * *note subring: subring, -- Constructs a subring of a polynomial ring.
  * *note RingElement % Subring: Reduction in subrings, -- Remainder modulo a
    subring
  * *note RingElement // Subring: RingElement // Subring, -- Subduction
    quotient with respect to a subring
  * *note sagbi: sagbi, -- Compute a subalgebra basis (sagbi basis)
  * *note groebnerMembershipTest: groebnerMembershipTest, -- Extrinsic method
    for subring membership

Ways to use groebnerSubductionQuotient:
=======================================

  * "groebnerSubductionQuotient(RingElement,Subring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note groebnerSubductionQuotient: groebnerSubductionQuotient, is a
*note method function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

