intersect(Subring,Subring) -- Intersection of subrings
******************************************************

  * Function: *note intersect: (Macaulay2Doc)intersect,
  * Usage: 
        result = intersect(S1, S2)
  * Inputs:
      * S1, a *note subring: Subring,, 
      * S2, a *note subring: Subring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: Subduction strategies, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Master", the update strategy at
        the beginning of each loop: "DegreeByDegree", "Incremental", and
        "Master". The strategy "Master" is a hybrid method that combines the
        other two; starting with "DegreeByDegree" for low degrees and switching
        to "Incremental".
      * *note SubductionMethod: SubductionMethod, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Top", the method used for
        subduction. *note SubductionMethod: SubductionMethod, can be either
        "Top" or "Engine".
      * *note SAGBILimitType: SAGBILimitType, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Fixed", Either "Fixed" or
        "Function". Determines the stopping criterion for the subalgebra bases
        computation. If "Fixed" then the *note Limit: Subduction computation
        limit, is used, otherwise, if "Function" is selected, then the maximum
        degree of the input generators is used as the degree limit.
      * *note Limit: Subduction computation limit, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 20, a degree limit for the binomial
        S-pairs that are computed internally.
      * *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value 0, which determines how much information is printed about
        the progress of the computation. Larger positive values of *note
        PrintLevel: PrintLevel, result in more output.
      * *note CheckFullIntersection: CheckFullIntersection, => a *note Boolean
        value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, which determines if
        *note isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, is run on the output
        *note IntersectedSubring: IntersectedSubring,.
      * *note Compute: Compute, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, which determines if the
        check to see if the computed generators form a subalgebra basis of the
        ring they generate is performed.
  * Outputs:
      * result, an *note intersected subring: IntersectedSubring,, 

Description
===========

Computes the intersection of input subrings of the same ambient ring.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^3 + x*y^2 + y^3);                                   |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = R/I;                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : S1 = subring {x^2, x*y};                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S2 = subring {x, y^2};                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : gens intersect(S1, S2, Limit=>5)                                |
|-- Warning! Result is not a full intersection.  Try increasing Limit.|
|                                                                     |
|o6 = | x2 x2y2+xy3 |                                                 |
|                                                                     |
|             1      2                                                |
|o6 : Matrix Q  <-- Q                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : S = intersect(S1, S2);                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : gens S                                                          |
|                                                                     |
|o8 = | x2 x2y2+xy3 y4 xy3 y6 xy5 |                                   |
|                                                                     |
|             1      6                                                |
|o8 : Matrix Q  <-- Q                                                 |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isFullIntersection S                                            |
|                                                                     |
|o9 = true                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : isSAGBI S                                                      |
|                                                                     |
|o10 = true                                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

The generators of the resulting *note IntersectedSubring: IntersectedSubring,
form a partial subalgebra basis for the computed intersection. When *note
CheckFullIntersection: CheckFullIntersection, is true, the function
automatically checks if the generators of the resulting *note
IntersectedSubring: IntersectedSubring, generate the intersection of the given
subrings. The generators of an instance of *note IntersectedSubring:
IntersectedSubring, lie in both input algebras. However, if the function cannot
guarantee that the generators of the resulting *note IntersectedSubring:
IntersectedSubring, generate the full intersection then a warning is given.

The function works by creating a composite subring $S$ from the input algebras
and attempts to compute a subalgebra basis for $S$. If a subalgebra basis $G$
for $S$ is found, then a subset of $G$ forms a subalgebra basis of the
intersection of the input algebras. Whenever this happens, the output is
guaranteed to be the full intersection of the input algebras and, furthermore,
form a subalgebra basis for the intersection. The function *note
isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, checks whether this is the case, i.e.,
whether a finite subalgebra basis for $S$ was found. If the function *note
isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, returns false then there are a few
different possibilities: First, the composite subring $S$ may have a finite
subalgebra basis that could be found by either setting the option *note
SAGBILimitType: SAGBILimitType, to its default value of Fixed or by using a
higher *note Limit: Subduction computation limit, option. Second, $S$ may not
have a finite subalgebra basis but the intersection does have a finite
subalgebra basis. In this case, the output may be a generating set for the full
intersection, but cannot be verified by the algorithm. Third, the intersection
of the input algebras may not have a finite subalgebra basis, and so the
composite subring does not have a finite subalgebra basis. In this case case,
the computed generators may be a generating set (but not a subalgebra basis)
for the intersection but the algorithm cannot guarantee it.

This function can also be run on a sequence containing both *note Subring:
Subring, and *note IntersectedSubring: IntersectedSubring, types. When *note
CheckFullIntersection: CheckFullIntersection, is true, all intermediate
intersections are checked for completeness.

+------------------------------+
|i11 : R = QQ[x,y];            |
+------------------------------+
|i12 : S1 = subring{x^2,y^3};  |
+------------------------------+
|i13 : S2 = subring{x,y^2};    |
+------------------------------+
|i14 : S3 = subring{x^4,y};    |
+------------------------------+
|i15 : gens intersect(S1,S2,S3)|
|                              |
|o15 = | x4 y6 |               |
|                              |
|              1      2        |
|o15 : Matrix R  <-- R         |
+------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
  * *note IntersectedSubring: IntersectedSubring, -- The type of all subrings
    arising from intersection
  * *note isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, -- check correctness of
    intersection computation
  * *note originalSubringGens: originalSubringGens, -- generators of the
    original subrings
  * *note isSAGBI: isSAGBI, -- Check if the generators are a subalgebra basis
  * *note Subduction computation limit: Subduction computation limit, -- Bound
    for subalgebra basis computation

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note intersect(Subring,Subring): intersect_lpSubring_cmSubring_rp, --
    Intersection of subrings
