IntersectedSubring -- The type of all subrings arising from intersection
************************************************************************

Description
===========

IntersectedSubring is a type of *note Subring: Subring, produced by
intersecting two subrings using the function *note intersect:
(Macaulay2Doc)intersect,. The function *note intersect:
(Macaulay2Doc)intersect, is the constructor for IntersectedSubring. Applying
the function *note isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, to an instance $S$
of IntersectedSubring checks whether the generators of $S$ are guaranteed to
generate the intersection of the original subrings.



+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S1 = subring{x^3,y};                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S2 = subring{x^2,y^2};                                  |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : S = intersect(S1,S2)                                    |
|                                                             |
|o4 = QQ[p_0..p_1], subring of R                              |
|                                                             |
|o4 : IntersectedSubring                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S#"originalSubrings"                                    |
|                                                             |
|o5 = {QQ[p_0..p_1], subring of R, QQ[p_0..p_1], subring of R}|
|                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

The originalSubrings field lists the two subrings which were used to generate
the intersection.

See also
========

  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
  * *note intersect(Subring,Subring): intersect_lpSubring_cmSubring_rp, --
    Intersection of subrings
  * *note isFullIntersection: isFullIntersection, -- check correctness of
    intersection computation
  * *note originalSubringGens: originalSubringGens, -- generators of the
    original subrings

Functions and methods returning an intersected subring:
=======================================================

  * *note intersect(Subring,Subring): intersect_lpSubring_cmSubring_rp, --
    Intersection of subrings

Methods that use an intersected subring:
========================================

  * "isFullIntersection(IntersectedSubring)" -- see *note isFullIntersection:
    isFullIntersection, -- check correctness of intersection computation
  * "originalSubringGens(IntersectedSubring)" -- see *note originalSubringGens:
    originalSubringGens, -- generators of the original subrings

For the programmer
