isSAGBI(SAGBIBasis) -- Check if the generators are a subalgebra basis
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note isSAGBI: isSAGBI,
  * Usage: 
        result = isSAGBI SB
  * Inputs:
      * SB, a *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Compute: Compute, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag indicating whether
        to perform computation.
      * *note Recompute: Recompute, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, if true then sagbiStatus
        is ignored and a computation is performed to verify if the subalgebra
        generators are a subalgebra basis.
      * *note Strategy: Subduction strategies, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Master", the update strategy used
        for updating the SAGBIBasis: "DegreeByDegree", "Incremental", and
        "Master". The strategy "Master" is a hybrid method that combines the
        other two; starting with "DegreeByDegree" for low degrees and switching
        to "Incremental".
      * *note SubductionMethod: SubductionMethod, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Top", the method used for
        subduction either: "Top" or "Engine".
      * *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value 0, When this is greater than zero, information is printed
        about the progress of the computation.
      * *note RenewOptions: RenewOptions, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, if true then the
        computation uses the options specified, otherwise it will use the
        previously selected options (except for the following, which may always
        be specified: *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel,, *note Limit: Subduction
        computation limit,, *note Recompute: Recompute,, and *note
        RenewOptions: RenewOptions,).
      * *note UseSubringGens: UseSubringGens, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, a flag indicating whether
        to use the generators of the subring of the partial subalgebra basis.
        If false then the method uses the subalgebra generators of the partial
        subalgebra basis.
      * *note ModifySAGBIBasis: ModifySAGBIBasis, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag indicating whether
        to replace the partial subalgebra basis cached in the subring.
  * Outputs:
      * result, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Checks whether the subalgebra generators of a *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis,
$SB$ form a subalgebra basis. The result of the computation is stored in the
sagbiStatus of $SB$. Subsequent calls of isSAGBI on $SB$ will look up the
result of the sagbiStatus unless the option *note Recompute: Recompute, is set
to true. If the option *note Compute: Compute, is set to false, then isSAGBI
attempts to find a previously cached result. If isSAGBI cannot determine a
result without computation and the option *note Compute: Compute, is set to
false, then isSAGBI returns null.

If the subalgebra generators of $SB$ form a subalgebra basis, then the partial
subalgebra basis is updated, unless *note ModifySAGBIBasis: ModifySAGBIBasis,
is set to false. If the option *note UseSubringGens: UseSubringGens, is set to
true, then the generators of the subring of $SB$ are used instead of the
subalgebra generators of the subring.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x+y+z,x*y+x*z+y*z, x*y*z, (x-y)*(x-z)*(y-z)};|
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isSAGBI S                                                 |
|                                                               |
|o3 = false                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isSAGBI sagbi(S, Limit => 5)                              |
|                                                               |
|o4 = false                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : S' = subring {x+y,x*y,x*y^2,x*y^7-y};                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isSAGBI S'                                                |
|                                                               |
|o6 = false                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isSAGBI sagbi(S', Limit => 5)                             |
|                                                               |
|o7 = false                                                     |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isSAGBI sagbi(S', Limit => 10)                            |
|                                                               |
|o8 = true                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

The options *note Subduction strategies: Subduction strategies,, *note
SubductionMethod: SubductionMethod,, *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel,, and *note
RenewOptions: RenewOptions, are only used when performing a subalgebra bases
computation.

