isSAGBI(Subring) -- Check if the generators are a subalgebra basis
******************************************************************

  * Function: *note isSAGBI: isSAGBI,
  * Usage: 
        result = isSAGBI S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note subring: Subring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Compute: Compute, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag indicating whether
        to perform computation.
      * *note Recompute: Recompute, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, if true then cached
        results are ignored and a computation is performed to verify if the
        generators are a subalgebra basis.
      * *note Strategy: Subduction strategies, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Master", the update strategy used
        for updating the SAGBIBasis: "DegreeByDegree", "Incremental", and
        "Master". The strategy "Master" is a hybrid method that combines the
        other two; starting with "DegreeByDegree" for low degrees and switching
        to "Incremental".
      * *note SubductionMethod: SubductionMethod, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Top", the method used for
        subduction either: "Top" or "Engine".
      * *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value 0, When this is greater than zero, information is printed
        about the progress of the computation.
      * *note RenewOptions: RenewOptions, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, if true then the
        computation will use the options specified, otherwise it will use the
        previously selected options (except for the following, which may always
        be specified: *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel,, *note Limit: Subduction
        computation limit,, *note Recompute: Recompute,, and *note
        RenewOptions: RenewOptions,)
      * *note UseSubringGens: UseSubringGens, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag indicating whether
        to use the generators of the subring. If false, then the method uses
        the subalgebra generators of the partial subalgebra basis.
      * *note ModifySAGBIBasis: ModifySAGBIBasis, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag indicating whether
        to replace the partial subalgebra basis cached in the subring.
  * Outputs:
      * result, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, if true, then
        the generators or subalgebra generators form a subalgebra basis.

Description
===========

Checks whether the generators of a *note subring: Subring, $S$ form a
subalgebra basis. The result of the computation is stored in the cache of the
ring. Subsequent calls to isSAGBI on $S$ with the same options will look up the
cached result unless the option *note Recompute: Recompute, is set to true. If
the option *note Compute: Compute, is set to false then isSAGBI attempts to
find a previously cached result. If isSAGBI cannot determine a result without
computation and the option *note Compute: Compute, is set to false, then
isSAGBI returns null.

If the generators of $S$ form a subalgebra basis, then the subalgebra
generators of the cached partial subalgebra basis are updated to match the ring
generators, unless the option *note ModifySAGBIBasis: ModifySAGBIBasis, is set
to false. If the option *note UseSubringGens: UseSubringGens, is set to false,
then the generators of a partial subalgebra basis are used instead of the
generators of the subring.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x+y+z,x*y+x*z+y*z, x*y*z, (x-y)*(x-z)*(y-z)};|
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
