File: SubalgebraBases.info, Node: presentationRing, Next: PrintLevel, Prev: originalSubringGens, Up: Top

presentationRing -- returns the presentation ring of a subring
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        presRing = presentationRing S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note subring: Subring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * presRing, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the
        presentation ring of S

Description
===========

Given a *note subring: Subring, $S$ of a *note quotient ring:
(Macaulay2Doc)QuotientRing, $Q$, the presentationRing $P$ is a polynomial ring
with the same coefficient ring as Q and with one variable for each generator of
S. There is a natural map from $P$ to $S$ that sends each variable to its
corresponding generator. Elements of the presentationRing represent polynomial
combinations of generators. Evaluating a polynomial combination of generators
is equal to applying this map. Therefore, $S$ is naturally isomorphic to the
quotient of $P$ by the kernel of the this map.

The presentationRing naturally arises when using *note RingElement // Subring:
RingElement // Subring,, which takes an element of a *note subring: Subring,
and expresses it as a polynomial combination of its generators.

Subrings include the field presentationMap, which provides a map from the
presentationRing to the *note ambient(Subring): ambient_lpSubring_rp, ring.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/2[x,y];                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : Q = R / ideal(x + y^5);       |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : S = subring {x+y, x*y, x*y^2};|
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : f = x^2*y^3 + x^4 + y^4;      |
+-----------------------------------+
|i5 : f % S                         |
|                                   |
|o5 = 0                             |
|                                   |
|o5 : Q                             |
+-----------------------------------+
|i6 : g = f // S                    |
|                                   |
|      4                            |
|o6 = p  + p p                      |
|      0    1 2                     |
|                                   |
|     ZZ                            |
|o6 : --[p ..p ]                    |
|      2  0   2                     |
+-----------------------------------+
|i7 : S#"presentationMap" g == f    |
|                                   |
|o7 = true                          |
+-----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
