File: SubalgebraBases.info, Node: Reduction in subrings, Next: RenewOptions, Prev: ReduceNewGenerators, Up: Top

Reduction in subrings -- Remainder modulo a subring
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = f % S
        R = M % S
        r = f % SB
        R = M % SB
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
      * S, a *note subring: Subring,, 
      * SB, a *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis,, 
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the normal form of
        f modulo the Subring or SAGBIBasis
      * R, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the normal form of entries of
        M modulo the subring or the SAGBIBasis

The result is zero if and only if the input belongs to the subring. If a
subalgebra basis is known for the subring, then subduction is used to compute
the normal forms. If no subalgebra basis is known, then an extrinsic method is
used, similar to groebnerMembershipTest.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x1, x2, x3];                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x1+x2+x3, x1*x2+x1*x3+x2*x3, x1*x2*x3,                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = QQ[p_0..p_3], subring of R                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Subring                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|(x1-x2)*(x1-x3)*(x2-x3)}                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = x1 + x2 + 2*x3                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = x1 + x2 + 2x3                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f % S                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = x3                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : g = x1^2*x2 + x2^2*x3 + x3^2*x1                                         |
|                                                                             |
|       2       2          2                                                  |
|o5 = x1 x2 + x2 x3 + x1*x3                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g % S                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = 0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
  * *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis, -- The type of all subalgebra bases
  * *note groebnerMembershipTest: groebnerMembershipTest, -- Extrinsic method
    for subring membership
