RingElement // Subring -- Subduction quotient with respect to a subring
***********************************************************************

  * Operator: *note //: (Macaulay2Doc)//,
  * Usage: 
        r = f // S
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
      * S, a *note subring: Subring,, 
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a subduction
        quotient of f with respect to the subring

Description
===========

The result is a ring element that lies in the *note presentationRing:
presentationRing, that has one variable for each generator of the subring $S$.
A subduction quotient is an expression of $f - (f\%S) \in S$ in terms of the
generators of $S$. The value of this element in the *note ambient(Subring):
ambient_lpSubring_rp, ring can be recovered using the field presentationMap of
the subring.

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                |
+---------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x+y,x*y,x*y^2};|
+---------------------------------+
|i3 : f = x^3;                    |
+---------------------------------+
|i4 : f - (f%S)                   |
|                                 |
|      3    2        2    3       |
|o4 = x  + x y + 2x*y  + y        |
|                                 |
|o4 : R                           |
+---------------------------------+
|i5 : gs = f // S                 |
|                                 |
|      3                          |
|o5 = p  - 2p p  + p              |
|      0     0 1    2             |
|                                 |
|o5 : QQ[p ..p ]                  |
|         0   2                   |
+---------------------------------+
|i6 : S#"presentationMap" gs      |
|                                 |
|      3    2        2    3       |
|o6 = x  + x y + 2x*y  + y        |
|                                 |
|o6 : R                           |
+---------------------------------+

This function calls *note groebnerSubductionQuotient:
groebnerSubductionQuotient,.

