SAGBIBasis -- The type of all subalgebra bases
**********************************************

Description
===========

A computation object for subalgebra bases. It stores a partial subalgebra bases
computation for picking up a computation where it left off. For many uses, it
is superior to use a *note subring: Subring,, as the computation SAGBIBases are
handled behind the scenes, and the user experience is more streamlined. To
create a *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis,, use the function *note sagbiBasis:
sagbiBasis,. The SAGBIBasis type is the main output type of the function *note
sagbi: sagbi,. Applying *note subring: subring, to a SAGBIBasis returns the
original subring that generated the SAGBIBasis.

See also
========

  * *note sagbiBasis: sagbiBasis, -- Constructs a computation object from a
    subring.
  * *note Subring: Subring, -- The type of all subrings
  * *note subring: subring, -- Constructs a subring of a polynomial ring.
  * *note sagbi: sagbi, -- Compute a subalgebra basis (sagbi basis)
  * *note generators(SAGBIBasis): generators_lpSAGBIBasis_rp, -- Returns
    generators of a SAGBIBasis computation object
  * *note status(SAGBIBasis): status_lpSAGBIBasis_rp, -- status of the
    subalgebra bases computation
  * *note numgens(SAGBIBasis): numgens_lpSAGBIBasis_rp, -- The number of
    generators of a SAGBIBasis

Functions and methods returning a SAGBIBasis:
=============================================

  * *note sagbi: sagbi, -- Compute a subalgebra basis (sagbi basis)
  * *note sagbiBasis: sagbiBasis, -- Constructs a computation object from a
    subring.

