subduction -- Subduction against a set elements
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = subduction(SB, M)
        n = subduction(SB, m)
        N = subduction(S, M)
        n = subduction(S, m)
        N = subduction(F, M)
        n = subduction(F, m)
        nList = subduction(FList, mList)
        n = subduction(FList, m)
  * Inputs:
      * SB, a *note SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis,, whose subalgebra generators are
        subducted against
      * S, a *note subring: Subring,, whose generators are subducted against
      * F, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, whose entries are subducted
        against
      * FList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, whose entries are subducted
        against
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a 1-row matrix whose entries
        are to be subducted
      * m, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the element to be
        subducted
      * mList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of elements to be
        subducted
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note AutoSubduce: AutoSubduce, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag indicating when to
        perform autosubduction on the generators before performing the
        Subalgebra basis computation
      * *note ReduceNewGenerators: ReduceNewGenerators, => a *note Boolean
        value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag indicating
        whether to reduce (via Gaussian elimination) to new subalgebra
        generators before adding them to the current subalgebra basis
      * *note StorePending: StorePending, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, a flag that indicates
        whether the pending list should be stored in the result.
      * *note Strategy: Subduction strategies, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Master", the update strategy at
        the beginning of each loop: "DegreeByDegree", "Incremental", and
        "Master". The strategy "Master" is a hybrid method that combines the
        other two; starting with "DegreeByDegree" for low degrees and switching
        to "Incremental".
      * *note SubductionMethod: SubductionMethod, => a *note string:
        (Macaulay2Doc)String,, default value "Top", the method used for
        subduction either: "Top" or "Engine".
      * *note Limit: Subduction computation limit, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 20, a degree limit for the binomial
        S-pairs that are computed internally.
      * *note AutoSubduceOnPartialCompletion: AutoSubduceOnPartialCompletion,
        => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false,
        apply autosubduction to the subalgebra generators the first time no new
        generators are added. Use this only if very few new subalgebra
        generators are expected.
      * *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,,
        default value 0, When this is greater than zero, information is printed
        about the progress of the computation
      * *note Recompute: Recompute, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, if true then the
        computation will resume, otherwise it starts at the beginning
      * *note RenewOptions: RenewOptions, => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, if true then the
        computation uses the options specified, otherwise it uses the
        previously selected options (except for the following, which may always
        be specified: *note PrintLevel: PrintLevel,, *note Limit: Subduction
        computation limit,, *note Recompute: Recompute,, and *note
        RenewOptions: RenewOptions,)
  * Outputs:
      * N, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, entries of $M$ after
        subduction
      * n, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the element $m$
        after subduction
      * nList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the elements of $mList$ after
        subduction

Description
===========

Performs subduction on the input with respect to the generating set of the
supplied object. The result of subduction of $f$ by $S$ is an element $g$ such
that $f-g$ is in $S$. If the generating set is not a subalgebra basis, then the
result of subduction may not be a normal form for the input.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : S = subring {x+y, x*y, x*y^2};|
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : f = x^4;                      |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : subduction(S, f)              |
|                                   |
|           3    4                  |
|o4 = - 2x*y  - y                   |
|                                   |
|o4 : R                             |
+-----------------------------------+
|i5 : sagbi S;                      |
+-----------------------------------+
|i6 : subduction(gens sagbi S, f)   |
|                                   |
|       4                           |
|o6 = -y                            |
|                                   |
|o6 : R                             |
+-----------------------------------+

