Subduction strategies -- Update procedure for the Sagbi algorithm
*****************************************************************

There are three possible values for Strategy: DegreeByDegree, Incremental, or
Master.

At the beginning of each loop inside of *note sagbi: sagbi,, the main *note
SAGBIBasis: SAGBIBasis, computation object is updated. There are two types of
update procedures, and the update procedure that is used is determined by the
value of Strategy.

The DegreeByDegree strategy computes a partial groebner basis of the reduction
ideal from scratch. The DegreeByDegree strategy is better when many new
generators are added during each loop of the *note sagbi: sagbi, algorithm. The
Incremental strategy computes a full groebner basis of the reduction ideal by
using the previous full groebner basis together with the data of the new
subalgebra generators. The Incremental strategy is better when there is little
change to the number of subalgebra generators.

For many examples, it is observed that many new generators are added at the
beginning of subalgebra basis computations, but, towards the end of the
computation, there are very few new generators that are added at each step. By
setting Strategy to Master (default), the DegreeByDegree strategy is used at
the beginning, and the strategy switches to Incremental part-of-the-way through
the algorithm.

